{
  "_comment": "Non-canonical medication status strings, each mapped to the FHIR R4 status code it means. Two match modes over the normalized key (lower-case, every run of non-alphanumerics to one space, trimmed; a key also matches when the two agree with spaces removed, so 'd/c' and 'dc' are one key): 'synonym' is a whole-string match, 'fragment' a contained-phrase match. The class a synonym implies is always its target code's class in medication-status-lifecycle; no synonym carries a class of its own. Collected from two places: the legacy spellings Cascade emitters and C-CDA imports are known to write, and the free-text status vocabulary an on-device extraction model emits. Every row lands as a candidate.",
  "rows": [
    { "text": "discontinued", "match": "synonym", "status": "stopped", "from": "legacy emitter spelling; named in the Cascade clinical vocabulary as the value that blocks a sh:in on medication status" },
    { "text": "inactive", "match": "synonym", "status": "stopped", "from": "C-CDA import and extraction writer spelling" },
    { "text": "canceled", "match": "synonym", "status": "cancelled", "from": "US spelling of the FHIR code" },
    { "text": "dc", "match": "synonym", "status": "stopped", "from": "clinical abbreviation; also matches d/c, whose key compacts to the same letters" },
    { "text": "dcd", "match": "synonym", "status": "stopped", "from": "clinical abbreviation (d/c'd)" },
    { "text": "stop", "match": "synonym", "status": "stopped", "from": "extraction model output" },
    { "text": "off", "match": "synonym", "status": "stopped", "from": "extraction model output" },
    { "text": "held", "match": "synonym", "status": "on-hold", "from": "extraction model output" },
    { "text": "hold", "match": "synonym", "status": "on-hold", "from": "extraction model output" },
